# width: 120
# env: PATH=${MNML_SHIMS}/ai:${PATH}
# env: TERM_PROGRAM=Hyper
# env: SHELL=/bin/sh
# The Settings overlay's two icon rows (`src/app/settings.zig`) read
# the live config: the bracket sits on `[figure]` / `[ghostty]` out of
# the box, and moves once a chip's `Icon` menu has written the key. A
# row that held a copy instead of reading `ui.claude_mark` back would
# show the stale value here.
#
# The disk write itself is `app/claude_mark.zig`'s unit tests (they can
# read the data root's config.zon, which lies outside the workspace
# this file can assert on, and they re-open an App on it to prove the
# key is read BACK). What this file proves is the round trip — menu →
# config → overlay → chrome, through the real key dispatcher.
#
# The filter is how the rows are reached, not a count of PgDn presses:
# they sit far enough down the UI section that any row added above them
# moves them, and `settings_filter.test` settled that a script should
# search for a row rather than scroll to a number that moves. `icon`
# leaves both of them on screen, the terminal's above the Claude one.
write a.txt "alpha alpha"
open a.txt
command view.settings_search
type icon
expect screen contains "Terminal icon:"
expect screen contains "Claude icon:"
expect screen contains "[ghostty] / terminal / custom"
expect screen contains "[figure] / spark"
key esc
key esc
expect screen lacks "Claude icon:"
# The Claude chip's `Icon ▸ Anthropic` (column 106, the strip's
# cluster).
rightclick 106 1
key end
key right
key down
key enter
expect screen contains "Claude icon: Anthropic spark"
command view.settings_search
type icon
expect screen contains "figure / [spark]"
# The terminal row is untouched by it — two keys, two rows.
expect screen contains "[ghostty] / terminal / custom"
key esc
key esc
# The terminal chip's `Icon ▸ Terminal`, the same shape. It sits three
# cells left of its usual column here: the Claude chip is in front of
# it on this strip.
rightclick 108 1
key end
key right
key down
key enter
expect screen contains "terminal icon: the codicon terminal"
command view.settings_search
type icon
expect screen contains "ghostty / [terminal] / custom"
expect screen contains "figure / [spark]"
key esc
key esc
